omply with Germany's  purity law the only ingredients used are  water  malted barley and hops workers here earn  around 450 euros a month that's more  than the statutory minimum wage but much  less than people earn elsewhere in  Europe most Georgians are in favor of  establishing closer ties with the EU  people expect it would give them a  better life and a higher standard of  living our country has good future  prospects with the EU and we can take  heart in the fact that things will get  better now we know where we belong along  with beer the brewery also makes sweet  carbonated drinks management is planning  to bring a new flavor onto the market  based on a traditional Georgian recipe  the organ mr. Georgia produces many  kinds of different carbonated drinks and  they drink them all the time  this is their latest innovation  chocolate cream  not even the brewery got its start with  a loan from the European Bank for  Reconstruction and Development  last year the EBRD loaned out some 214  million euros to help Georgia modernize  at its annual meeting the bank's  director for the Caucasus Moldova and  Belarus explains what needs to be done  he needs to transcend its institutions  he need to strengthen also its  regulatory body and in general he needs  to do to continue modernizing the  economy bringing new technologies making  its economy more competitive and attract  investments also to improve improve  employment I think Georgia is doing the  right thing but Martina shvarts says it  will take years before these positive  changes will be felt by the general  population reforms are underway but  Georgia still has a long way to go
 

